)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{8}.\n$$" 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679197 1075 #edb/ref 17592186679141 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679197 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679197 1077 "answer" 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679197 1078 #edb/ref 17592186679141 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679197 1079 #uuid "f0e7ca9e-841b-531b-a4f0-3cbddc3883f2" 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679198 1068 #edb/ref 17592186679205 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679198 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679198 1071 "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679198 1072 #uuid "f3812e4c-4072-5cbb-aae5-d8098598e7d2" 13194139539879 17592186576411 true] [17592186679198 1074 "Let $u